  "text": "File\nEdit\nView\nHelp\nNew Agent\nCtrl+N\nAutomations\nMarketplace\nRepositories\nsakura-diorama\n3d pixel art diorama design\n8m\nHome\nNo agents yet\nIW\nIgor Warzocha\nFree Plan\nChat title.\n3d pixel art diorama design\n\nis that the best you can do? this is fake 3d. And I asked for high quality pixel art, modern. Not nes era 320x240.\n\nThought\nfor 9s\n\nRebuilding with real Three.js voxel 3D, a higher-resolution pixel pipeline, and a modern pixel-art look—not flat isometric canvas.\n\nExplored\n1 file, 1 search\n\nRebuilding with real Three.js voxel geometry, instanced meshes, proper lighting, and a modern high-res pixel render pipeline (not flat isometric canvas).\n\nEdited\nindex.html\n+608\n-755\n\nFixing the render pipeline (proper 3D → pixel buffer → screen) and polishing materials and scene detail.\n\nEdited\n2 files, ran 2 commands\n+63\n-58\nMonitored background task\n1 active\nWaited\n35s\nRead\nterminal\nRead\nsakura3d.png\nThought\nfor 11s\n\nScene didn't render — likely a Three.js API issue. Fixing and adding error reporting.\n\nExplored\n1 search, ran 1 command\n\nEmpty canvas — likely UniformsUtils removal in Three.js r170. Fixing that and hardening startup.\n\nEdited\nindex.html, explored 1 file, ran 1 command\n+16\n-3\nMonitored background task\n1 active\n\nHeadless screenshot failed due to no WebGL GPU (environment limitation). Polishing the scene and adding WebGL detection so it runs properly in a real browser.\n\nEdited\nindex.html\n+48\n-8\n\nYou're right to push back on the first version — it was fake 3D (2D isometric canvas at 320×240). That’s been replaced entirely.\n\nWhat’s different now\nReal 3D — Three.js instanced voxel cubes in world space with perspective camera, shadows, and orbit/zoom\nModern pixel pipeline — scene renders at 1280×720, then upscales with nearest-neighbor + light dither and 32-level color quantization (not NES resolution)\nCel-shaded voxels — MeshToonMaterial with gradient map for a contemporary pixel-art look (closer to games like Eastward / voxel showcases)\nDenser scene — ~1100 blossom voxels, koi, clouds, toon lighting, dusk lantern glow, 3D petal planes\nOpen it\nxdg-open /home/igorw/Projects/sakura-diorama/index.html\n\nNeeds network once for the Three.js CDN. Use a normal browser with GPU/WebGL — headless screenshots here fail with “WebGL context” errors; your desktop browser should be fine.\n\nDrag to orbit in true 3D, scroll to zoom. Buttons: Petals, Dusk, Bloom, Reset camera.\n\nIf it still feels too “chunky” or not polished enough on your machine, say whether you want finer voxels, higher pixel buffer (e.g. 1920×1080), or hand-painted texture atlases on the meshes — those are the next quality steps.\n\nWill resume when background work finishes\n6 Terminals\nReview\n+832\nReview\n+832\n\n\n\n\nAuto\n\nLocal\nmaster\n29% context",
